-- DICT-SEMANTICS §4 `var` + `gen-sig` (#619): the ENFORCEMENT half of
-- s4-gen-sig-declared-context-kept. Identical program, violating call site.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER (hand-derived): `var` discharges each residual predicate of the
-- instantiated scheme. `sz2 "hi"` instantiates `a := String`; `match(IE, Sz
-- String)` is empty and no assumption is in scope, so the goal is unentailed and
-- the program is REJECTED. Discharge is keyed off the binding's DECLARED
-- context, not off whether the body happened to contain a method occurrence --
-- and this body contains none, which is the whole point.
--
-- OBSERVED: check/run/build all REJECT with `T-NO-IMPL` ("No impl of Sz for
-- String"). CONFORMANT.
--
-- LEDGER: #610 (S2, CLOSED) -- this program passed `check` at exit 0.
-- Its control lives in s4-gen-sig-declared-context-kept: the same binding with a
-- SATISFIED call. Neither row alone distinguishes "the declared context is
-- enforced" from "nothing is ever enforced"/"everything is rejected".
interface Sz a where
  sz : a -> Int

impl Sz Int where
  sz n = n

sz2 : Sz a => a -> Int
sz2 x = 9

main = println (sz2 "hi")
